{{!
    @template mod_edpreset/reorder_item

    One activity in the section template reorder dialogue.

    Rendered identically in both columns, because an item keeps its own identity when it is dragged
    across: the pill says where the activity came from, not which column it is sitting in.

    Only the teacher's own activities are draggable. A template's activities are shown in the order
    its curator arranged them and stay there, so they get no drag handle - core/drag_handle's
    data-drag-type="move" is what core/sortable_list looks for, and without it a drag never starts.
    A blank handle-sized spacer takes its place so both kinds of row line up.

    Plain divs rather than an li, and with no list ARIA roles, because the Mustache linter renders
    this partial on its own and either an li or a role="listitem" is invalid without its container.
    core/sortable_list does not care what the elements are - core's own callers use table rows - and
    the interaction that matters for assistive technology is the drag handle below, which is a
    labelled button and opens core/sortable_list's own keyboard move dialogue.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * token string - p<presetid> for a template activity, c<cmid> for one already in the course
    * name string - the name the activity will have
    * modfullname string - the human-readable activity type, e.g. "Book"
    * icon string - pre-rendered icon HTML
    * modname string - the activity's module, for the icon container
    * purpose string - the activity's MOD_PURPOSE_*, which colours the icon
    * branded bool - whether the icon is branded and must not be recoloured
    * istemplate bool - whether this activity comes from the template
    * movetitle string - the drag handle's label; core/drag_handle takes it as a plain variable.
      Unused for a template activity, which has no handle.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "token": "p7",
        "name": "Weekly reading",
        "modfullname": "Book",
        "icon": "<img src='#' alt=''>",
        "modname": "book",
        "purpose": "content",
        "branded": false,
        "istemplate": true,
        "movetitle": "Move Weekly reading"
    }
}}
<div class="edpreset-reorder-item {{#istemplate}}edpreset-reorder-item-template{{/istemplate}}{{^istemplate}}edpreset-reorder-item-course{{/istemplate}}"
     data-token="{{token}}"
>
    {{! Only the teacher's own activities get a handle. core/sortable_list refuses to start a drag
        unless the mousedown landed inside its moveHandlerSelector, so leaving the handle off is what
        pins the template's activities in the order the curator set. They are still perfectly good
        drop positions: the list builds destinations from its children, handle or no handle. }}
    {{#istemplate}}
        <span class="edpreset-reorder-handle edpreset-reorder-handle-fixed" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="fa-stack">
                <i class="icon fa fa-solid fa-arrows-up-down-left-right fa-fw fa-stack-1x" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <i class="icon fa fa-solid fa-ban fa-stack-1x fa-xs"></i>
            </span>
        </span>
    {{/istemplate}}
    {{^istemplate}}
        <span class="edpreset-reorder-handle">
            {{> core/drag_handle }}
        </span>
    {{/istemplate}}
    <div class="w-100">
        <div class="edpreset-reorder-name">{{name}}</div>
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center justify-content-between">
            <div class="d-flex align-items-center edpreset-modinfo">
                <div class="edpreset-card-icon icon-no-margin modicon_{{modname}} activityiconcontainer smaller {{purpose}} isbranded me-1">
                    {{{icon}}}
                </div>
                <small class="text-muted">{{modfullname}}</small>
            </div>
            {{#istemplate}}
                <span class="edpreset-tag edpreset-pill edpreset-pill-template"
                    data-toggle="tooltip"
                    title="{{#str}} reorder:templatepill_help, mod_edpreset {{/str}}"
                >{{#str}} reorder:templatepill, mod_edpreset {{/str}}</span>
            {{/istemplate}}
            <!--{{^istemplate}}
                <span class="edpreset-tag edpreset-pill edpreset-pill-existing"
                    data-toggle="tooltip"
                    title="{{#str}} reorder:existingpill_help, mod_edpreset {{/str}}"
                >{{#str}} reorder:existingpill, mod_edpreset {{/str}}</span>
            {{/istemplate}}-->
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
